From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DeepSeek Harness <noreply@deepseek.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:34:48 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the rubber band choosing what the list's edge covers
 when the pointer is dragged out of the list and end it from any release in
 the window, since a drag that left the page froze its choice or stuck the
 band, and widen the choosing rectangle to 1 DIP so a straight drag picks the
 rows it crosses.

---
 AGENTS.md                |   2 +-
 CHANGELOG.md             |   2 +
 CLAUDE.md                |   2 +-
 README.md                |   2 +-
 app/browser.go           | 128 ++++++++++--
 app/files.go             |  16 ++
 app/grid.go              |   4 +
 app/marqueerange_test.go | 407 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 8 files changed, 543 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 app/marqueerange_test.go

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 44dedf7..7a062ad 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -104,4 +104,4 @@ Entering the page reads the cache again only when it is entered (`dedupEnter` no
 - `Painter.AnimationFrame` (and `After`) only paints the window again: the view is not built, so anything computed while building (an element's size, an effect's uniforms, state moved on in `View`) stands still in those frames. Read the time as you paint (`p.Now()` in a `Draw` callback, or in an effect's `PaintEffect`, as `specksFx` does), and call `c.Invalidate()` while something built must move (`a.moving()`). Stamp an animation's start in the first frame that shows it, not from the last frame built, which may be long past.
 - Files come and go through specks (`app/arrivals.go`): a deleted file stays in its listing while it dissolves (`a.dying`, kept through reloads by `keepDying`), and an upload shows in its folder at once as a row with a negative FsID that gathers as its bytes go up (`a.gathers`, by the path of the entry it makes); rows with a negative FsID or dissolving are never chosen or opened.
 - Sidebar icons are drawn in code (`app/navicons.go`) so their parts can move; `navGlyph` takes the time into the gesture. A page's icon plays once when the page opens (`a.navRun`).
-- The browser's pointer gestures (`marquee` and the move drag in `app/browser.go`): the page's `ObserveInput` (the capture phase) sees every pointer press, move and release in it, in window coordinates (`page.PointerPosition` plus the page's box). A press on a row or a grid tile — `l.rowRects`, filled each frame with each list row's `Bounds`, and `gridSpot.rect` — begins a move drag once the pointer goes `marqueeSlop` DIPs: it drags the whole choice when the pressed item is one of it, else it chooses just that item and drags it (a plain click still chooses by MyGo's `ListState`). While dragging, `page.DrawOver` paints a translucent card that follows the pointer (icon + name, or "N 项") and lights the folder under it (`l.moveTarget`/`l.moveTargetRect`: a folder row, a folder tile, or a breadcrumb from `l.crumbRects`); the release moves the files with `moveOrCopyAfter`, refusing the same folder, the folder itself and its own subfolders, and asking `place` about clashing names, while a release on blank space or off the window cancels. A press on the list's or grid's blank space instead paints the rubber band — a faint `t.Accent.Alpha(0.12)` fill and a 1px `t.Accent` stroke, rounded, clipped to `l.dragArea` — and chooses the rows (`l.rowRects`) or tiles (`gridSpot.rect`) it intersects, replacing the choice or, with Cmd held at the press, adding to it (`l.dragBase`); a blank-space press let go without dragging (both of the box's sides under `marqueeSlop`) is a click on empty space, which clears the choice (`l.sel.Clear()`, `l.selected = -1`) unless Cmd was held at the press, which adds and keeps it; MyGo's `ListState.DragSelect` is off. A release over the title bar is not under the page, so `filesToolbar`'s own `ObserveInput` ends a drag dropped on a breadcrumb or let go over the tools, and a canceled or fresh press clears any leftover state. Both gestures are hidden while the preview, a dialog, an in-place rename or the folder maker has the pointer, and while files from another app are dragged in (`l.over`).
+- The browser's pointer gestures (`marquee` and the move drag in `app/browser.go`): the page's `ObserveInput` (the capture phase) sees every pointer press in it, in window coordinates (its box plus the event's local point), and the root's `ObserveInput` sees every release in the window, so letting go over the title bar or the sidebar — not under the page — still ends the gesture (`a.pointerUp`, which also drops a dragged file there) and clears the band; while a gesture runs the pointer's place comes from `c.Root().PointerPosition()`, the column covering the whole window, so moves off the page still reach the view (the page alone gets none), with `l.dragAt` keeping the last place seen on the window for a frame that tells none, and `l.gestureEl` (this frame's list or grid) ending a band whose press the window saw go while the pointer was off the window. A press on a row or a grid tile — `l.rowRects`, filled each frame with each list row's `Bounds`, and `gridSpot.rect` — begins a move drag once the pointer goes `marqueeSlop` DIPs: it drags the whole choice when the pressed item is one of it, else it chooses just that item and drags it (a plain click still chooses by MyGo's `ListState`). While dragging, `page.DrawOver` paints a translucent card that follows the pointer (icon + name, or "N 项") and lights the folder under it (`l.moveTarget`/`l.moveTargetRect`: a folder row, a folder tile, or a breadcrumb from `l.crumbRects`); the release moves the files with `moveOrCopyAfter`, refusing the same folder, the folder itself and its own subfolders, and asking `place` about clashing names, while a release on blank space or off the window cancels. A press on the list's or grid's blank space instead paints the rubber band — a faint `t.Accent.Alpha(0.12)` fill and a 1px `t.Accent` stroke, rounded, clipped to `l.dragArea` — and chooses the rows (`l.rowRects`) or tiles (`gridSpot.rect`) it intersects, replacing the choice or, with Cmd held at the press, adding to it (`l.dragBase`); its pointer is clamped to the choice's area first (`choiceArea`: `l.dragArea` widened to the furthest row or tile edge, `l.contentBottom`/`l.contentRight`, as the list pads its foot 16 DIP and its sides 10), so a pointer dragged past the list's edge parks the box on the edge and the choice is what that edge covers, and the choosing rectangle is widened to at least 1 DIP each way around a line (`choiceRect`), so a drag straight up, down or across still crosses the rows or tiles it goes through (a zero-width rectangle crosses none by `rectIntersects`' strict test); the choice is recomputed only when that clamped rectangle changes (`l.dragLast`), so hanging past the edge costs no scan; a blank-space press let go without dragging (both of the box's sides under `marqueeSlop`) is a click on empty space, which clears the choice (`l.sel.Clear()`, `l.selected = -1`) unless Cmd was held at the press, which adds and keeps it; MyGo's `ListState.DragSelect` is off. A release over the title bar is not under the page, so `filesToolbar`'s own `ObserveInput` ends a drag dropped on a breadcrumb or let go over the tools as well, and a canceled or fresh press clears any leftover state. Both gestures are hidden while the preview, a dialog, an in-place rename or the folder maker has the pointer, and while files from another app are dragged in (`l.over`).
